<title>USA: Swiss Bank NY Branch sells $300 mln 20-yr notes.</title>
<headline>Swiss Bank NY Branch sells $300 mln 20-yr notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Swiss Bank Corp NY Branch was priced on Tuesday via Swiss Bank</p>
<p>Corp, according to a syndicate source.</p>
<p>BORROWER SWISS BANK CORP NY BRANCH</p>
<p>AMT $300 MLN	COUPON 7.375 PCT   MATURITY 6/15/2017</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	  ISS PRICE 98.775   FIRST PAY DATE 12/15/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S AA2  YIELD 7.494 PCT    PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>S&amp;P AA		SPREAD 62 BPS	CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678</p>
</text>
